# Build context exclusion for the API image (root Dockerfile).
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS AT ALL
#   Docker sends the whole context to the daemon before it builds. This repo has
#   a node_modules tree at the root and a second, larger one inside dashboard/;
#   without these rules every API build uploads both, and .env — which holds
#   every live credential — would be uploaded too.

# Secrets. `.env.example` stays: it is a template with no real values, and it
# documents what the image needs at run time.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Generated post images: belong to the running container's volume, not the image.
media/

# Installed in the build stage from package-lock.json.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# The dashboard is its own image with its own context (dashboard/Dockerfile).
# Excluding it here keeps the API's build cache stable — a dashboard edit should
# not invalidate the API image.
dashboard

# Not needed at run time: the tests, the design docs, and the slide deck.
tests
docs
slide.md

# Version control and local tooling state.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.commandcode
sdkprobe

# Noise.
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
